# Use Cases

100 questions total, **unevenly distributed** — each use case gets the count its scenario demands. Sorted by Normain mode. UC IDs are stable identifiers.

**Uniqueness** = how much of this test exercises capabilities that aren't already covered by another use case. Higher = more distinctive contribution. Subjective.

| # | Use case | Mode | Persona | Scenario | Question types | # docs | # questions | Uniqueness | What it tests |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 01 | Due diligence financial review | Simple | PE / corp dev analyst reviewing a target | Verify financials, spot red flags, cross-check numbers between annual report, proxy, and Excel model | Numerical calc; cross-doc (10-K vs proxy); Excel step-by-step logic; reasoning on covenants/warning signs | 6 | 15 | **30%** — Excel logic unique; numerical + cross-doc overlap with several others | Numeric extraction + cross-doc consistency + chained reasoning |
| 06 | Multimodal evidence extraction | Simple | Advisory / forensic analyst | Single mixed-format corpus; varied Qs pull facts from scans, photos, charts, handwriting | OCR-grade text from scans; handwriting recognition; image-only chart interpretation; cross-modal reconciliation | 4 | 10 | **90%** — only test covering scanned, handwritten, image-only formats | Format coverage — exposes tools that can't ingest non-text inputs |
| 07 | M&A data-room deep dive | Simple | M&A counsel / investment committee chair | 10 deep synthesis questions over a target's full data room (red flags, hidden liabilities, change-of-control exposure, IP issues, regulatory risk, key-employee dependencies, customer concentration, litigation, off-balance-sheet items, MAC triggers) | Synthesis across many docs; risk identification; pattern detection; gap identification at scale | **100+** | 10 | **85%** — depth × scale combo; tests context-window survival + lost-in-the-middle; no other UC stresses this | Reasoning across very large corpora — Normain's strongest competitive wedge |
| 02 | ESG / sustainability audit | Repeat | Sustainability lead prepping CSRD, or auditor | Same Qs across multiple companies' sustainability reports → comparison table | Exhaustive search; numerical aggregation; multi-doc cross-reference (report vs framework) | 4 | 15 | **35%** — framework-vs-disclosure alignment angle | Long-doc exhaustive extraction + framework alignment |
| 04 | Contract clause sweep at scale | Repeat | Legal ops / M&A counsel | Same clause-finding Qs across **100+ contracts** in a bundle → per-contract comparison table. Real-customer scale; most competitors choke past 20–50 files | Exhaustive (find every X); classification; clause-level citation fidelity; cross-contract pattern detection | **100+** | 20 | **70%** — only Repeat-at-scale test; exposes per-doc-count limits in competitors; clause-level citation fidelity at scale | Repeat-mode scale ceiling + accurate clause-level citation across hundreds of docs |
| 03 | Regulatory-vs-policy gap check | Spreadsheet | GRC / internal audit | Each row = one obligation from the regulation; columns assess policy coverage with citations | Cross-doc (reg vs policy); exhaustive requirements enumeration; classification; reasoning on partial coverage | 6 | 15 | **55%** — per-obligation structured enumeration unique; cross-doc + exhaustive overlap others | Cross-doc reasoning + exhaustiveness + citation fidelity |
| 05 | Vendor / supplier risk matrix | Spreadsheet | GRC / vendor management / TPRM lead | Each row = one vendor; columns score risk dimensions (data handling, breach history, cert status, sub-processor exposure) using vendor's SOC2 + public disclosures + ToS | Cross-doc per vendor; classification (risk tier); per-column varied questions; citation across short security docs | ~15 | 15 | **65%** — vendor TPRM scenario unique; partial overlap with UC03 (Spreadsheet) and UC04 (legal-doc parsing) | Per-row varied prompting + cross-doc per entity + risk classification |

**Total**: 7 use cases, 100 questions, ~235+ docs (UC04 + UC07 dominate doc count).

## Mode coverage

- **Simple** (3): UC01, UC06, UC07
- **Repeat** (2): UC02, UC04
- **Spreadsheet** (2): UC03, UC05

All three Normain modes covered. Tilted toward Simple to include the new depth-at-scale test (UC07), which is most differentiating.

## Scale stress points

| Stress | Use case | Why it matters |
|---|---|---|
| **Many questions, few docs** | UC04 (20 Qs × 100 contracts), UC07 (10 Qs × 100 docs) | Real per-corpus question volume |
| **Many docs, repeat mode** | UC04 (100+ contracts), UC05 (15 vendor docs) | Per-doc context isolation at scale |
| **Few questions, deep synthesis** | UC07 (10 deep Qs spanning the whole room) | Lost-in-the-middle, citation drift, context overflow |
| **Multimodal** | UC06 | Format ingestion ceiling |
